// Polkit rule for shepherd's session watchdog (issue #172).
//
// Every activity runs as the kiosk uid, and so does `shepherdd`. Signal
// permission is a uid comparison, so an activity can `kill` -- or `SIGSTOP` --
// the daemon supervising it, and the session carries on with no time
// accounting, no bedtime and no audit. The fallback that catches a shepherdd
// which merely *exits* (`sh -c '... || loginctl terminate-session'`, installed
// into the sway config) runs at that same uid, so killing it first defeats it.
//
// The one part of shepherd outside the session is the state custodian,
// `shepherd-stated`, running as `shepherd-state`: a uid nothing inside the
// session can signal, and which already knows which logind session is the
// kiosk's. It watches a connection `shepherdd` holds open and ends the session
// when the feeding stops. Ending a session it does not own is what this rule
// grants.
//
// Install path: /etc/polkit-1/rules.d/50-shepherd-session-guard.rules
//
// ## What this widens, said plainly
//
// polkit passes no details for `TerminateSession`, so this cannot be narrowed
// to one session or one user: it grants `shepherd-state` the right to end ANY
// session on this machine, an administrator's SSH login included. What keeps
// that acceptable is the shape of the daemon holding it -- no network, no
// subprocesses, `ProtectSystem=strict`, one call site, and a session id it
// resolved from logind (class=user, type=wayland, seated, not closing) rather
// than took from the wire. Nothing at the kiosk uid can reach it: not the
// directory, not the socket, not the process.
//
// Without this rule the device still boots and everything else still works.
// The custodian checks for it at startup, `shepherdd` raises the `Critical`
// diagnostic `session_not_guarded`, and the journal names this file -- because
// a watchdog that cannot fire is worse than none: it is the shape that looks
// like protection.

polkit.addRule(function(action, subject) {
    if (action.id === "org.freedesktop.login1.manage" &&
        subject.user === "shepherd-state") {
        return polkit.Result.YES;
    }
});
